# [P0-6 AUDIT 2026-09] Firmware binaries are NOT source — they are immutable
# build artifacts owned by the Firmware-Backend repo. The PWA must NOT track
# its own binary copy (audit-7: a 144-byte drift existed between the PWA's
# committed v1.7.1 and the firmware repo's v1.7.1). The release_firmware_
# generic.py script (in the firmware repo) syncs verified-SHA binaries into
# public/firmware/ at release time. The manifest.json IS tracked (small,
# text) but binary payloads are gitignored and pulled on-demand.
public/firmware/*.bin
public/firmware/*.bin.sha256
public/firmware/*.bin.sig
public/firmware/*.bin.ota.json
public/firmware/SHA256SUMS
public/firmware/release.json
public/firmware/provenance.json

# Runtime/mocks
.data/
dev.log
server.log
3100
.vercel
.env*
